      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the structure. The original test contains a massive amount of irrelevant infrastructure code copied from a base test class. The actual test method is just 3 lines. I'll create a lean, focused test that strips all the noise and makes the intent immediately clear.Let me check where `IntegerTransformer` is defined.Now I have everything I need. I'll write a clean, focused test that strips the irrelevant infrastructure and makes the intent obvious.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version strips ~500 lines of irrelevant infrastructure down to a focused 40-line class: it defines only the `IntegerTransformer` needed to construct the collection, then clearly comments each step of the test — key-not-present first insert succeeds, duplicate key second insert must throw `IllegalArgumentException`."
